  "result": "Perfect! All 169 tests pass (153 existing + 16 new statement tests). Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Customer Statements Implementation\n\n**src/statements.js** \u2014 New module with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function:\n\n- **Input validation**:\n  - Normalizes customer ID\n  - Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customers\n\n- **Invoice filtering**:\n  - Only includes invoices for the specified customer\n  - Only includes invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes drafts and paid invoices)\n  - Only includes invoices with `issueDate` on or before `asOf` date\n\n- **Return format**: `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n  - `invoices`: Array of invoice objects, each with:\n    - `number`: Invoice number\n    - `issueDate`: Issue date\n    - `dueDate`: Payment due date\n    - `total`: Total amount (from `invoiceTotals`)\n    - `due`: Balance due (from `balanceDue`)\n  - Sorted by `issueDate` (oldest first)\n  - `totalDue`: Sum of all `due` amounts\n\n**test/statements.test.js** \u2014 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Basic statement generation with outstanding invoices\n- Total due calculation\n- Customer ID normalization\n- Unknown customer error handling\n- Date filtering (before, on, and after asOf)\n- Draft invoice exclusion\n- Paid invoice exclusion\n- Other customer invoice exclusion\n- Sorting by issue date\n- Multiple invoice handling\n- Partial payment scenarios\n- Total calculation integration\n- Due date inclusion\n- Mixed customer scenarios\n\nAll 169 tests pass.",
